Cross Encoder is called a relevance score. It represents how relevant a retrieved document is to the user's query. 
The reranker uses these scores to reorder the retrieved documents so
that the most relevant chunks are sent to the LLM. It is different from cosine similarity, which is used during vector sear

Retriever → Reranker → LLM

The retriever finds candidates quickly; the cross encoder acts like a judge that picks the best candidates before the LLM answers.

